s":"hollow"},{"surface":"பள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"பள்ளி","lemma":"பள்ளி","gloss":"resting place"}],"gloss":"resting place"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அலவன்","parts":[{"text":"அலவன்","lemma":"அலவன்","gloss":"crab"}],"gloss":"crab"},{"surface":"சிறு","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"}],"gloss":"small"},{"surface":"மனை","parts":[{"text":"மனை","lemma":"மனை","gloss":"house"}],"gloss":"house"},{"surface":"சிதைய","parts":[{"text":"சிதை","lemma":"சிதை","gloss":"destroy"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to be destroyed"},{"surface":"புணரி","parts":[{"text":"புணரி","lemma":"புணரி","gloss":"wave"}],"gloss":"wave"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குணில்","parts":[{"text":"குணில்","lemma":"குணில்","gloss":"drumstick"}],"gloss":"drumstick"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"edge/mouth"}],"gloss":"edge/mouth"},{"surface":"முரசின்","parts":[{"text":"முரசு","lemma":"முரசு","gloss":"drum"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"like/of"}],"gloss":"like a drum"},{"surface":"இயங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இயங்கு","lemma":"இயங்கு","gloss":"move/sound"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"moving/sounding"},{"surface":"துறைவன்","parts":[{"text":"துறை","lemma":"துறை","gloss":"shore"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"masculine singular suffix"}],"gloss":"lord of the shore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நல்கிய","parts":[{"text":"நல்கு","lemma":"நல்கு","gloss":"grant"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"granted"},{"surface":"நாள்","parts":[{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"நாள்","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"days"},{"surface":"தவ","parts":[{"text":"தவ","lemma":"தவ","gloss":"very"}],"gloss":"very"},{"surface":"சிலவே","parts":[{"text":"சில","lemma":"சில","gloss":"few"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"are few indeed"},{"surface":"அலரே","parts":[{"text":"அலர்","lemma":"அலர்","gloss":"gossip"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"but the gossip"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வில்","parts":[{"text":"வில்","lemma":"வில்","gloss":"bow"}],"gloss":"bow"},{"surface":"கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"கெழு","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"possessing"},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"தானை","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"army"},{"surface":"விச்சியர்","parts":[{"text":"விச்சியர்","lemma":"விச்சியர்","gloss":"Vicciyar clan"}],"gloss":"of the Vicciyar"},{"surface":"பெருமகன்","parts":[{"text":"பெரு","lemma":"பெரு","gloss":"great"},{"text":"மகன்","lemma":"மகன்","gloss":"son/chief"}],"gloss":"great chief"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேந்தரொடு","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தர்","lemma":"வேந்தர்","gloss":"kings"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"ஒடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with the kings"},{"surface":"பொருத","parts":[{"text":"பொரு","lemma":"பொரு","gloss":"fight"},{"text":"த","lemma":"த","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"fought"},{"surface":"ஞான்றை","parts":[{"text":"ஞான்று","lemma":"ஞான்று","gloss":"time"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"at the time of"},{"surface":"பாணர்","parts":[{"text":"பாணர்","lemma":"பாணர்","gloss":"bards"}],"gloss":"bards"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புலி","parts":[{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"}],"gloss":"tiger"},{"surface":"நோக்கு","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கு","lemma":"நோக்கு","gloss":"look/gaze"}],"gloss":"gaze"},{"surface":"உறழ்","parts":[{"text":"உறழ்","lemma":"உறழ்","gloss":"resemble/vie"}],"gloss":"resembling"},{"surface":"நிலை","parts":[{"text":"நிலை","lemma":"நிலை","gloss":"stance"}],"gloss":"stance"},{"surface":"கண்ட","parts":[{"text":"கண்ட","lemma":"கண்ட","gloss":"who saw"}],"gloss":"who saw","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கலி","parts":[{"text":"கலி","lemma":"கலி","gloss":"noise/uproar"}],"gloss":"noise"},{"surface":"கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"கெழு","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"possessing"},{"surface":"குறும்பூர்","parts":[{"text":"குறும்பூர்","lemma":"குறும்பூர்","gloss":"Kurumpur town"}],"gloss":"Kurumpur"},{"surface":"ஆர்ப்பினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்ப்பு","lemma":"ஆர்ப்பு","gloss":"clamor"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"comparative"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even more than the clamor"},{"surface":"பெரிதே","parts":[{"text":"பெரிது","lemma":"பெரிது","gloss":"great thing"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is greater indeed"}]}],"literal":"Small-flowered ñāḻal tree's root-hollow resting place / of the crab, its small house, so as to destroy, the wave / like a drum struck by a drumstick, moves, the lord of the shore; / the days he granted us are very few, but the public gossip / is like the bow-bearing army's chief of the Vicciyar, / when he fought with the kings, the bards / who saw the tiger-like fierce stance, / raised a clamor in noisy Kurumpur, and this gossip is even greater than that!","translation":"The waves crash like drums struck by drumsticks, destroying the tiny homes built by crabs in the hollows of the roots of the small-flowered ñāḻal trees on the shore of our lord. The days he spent lovingly with us are very few indeed. Yet, the gossip about us is louder than the great uproar that rose in the noisy town of Kurumpur, when the bards witnessed the fierce, tiger-like battle stance of the great chief of the bow-wielding Vicciyar army fighting against the great kings.","modern":"சிறிய பூக்களைக் கொண்ட ஞாழல் மரத்தின் வேர் வளைகளில் நண்டுகள் கட்டிய சிறிய வீடுகள் அழியும்படி, முரசு போல ஒலிக்கும் அலைகள் மோதும் கடற்கரைத் தலைவன் நம்மோடு கூடி மகிழ்ந்த நாட்கள் மிகச் சிலவே. ஆனால், வில்லேந்திய படையையுடைய விச்சியர் தலைவன் மூவேந்தர்களுடன் போரிட்டபோது, அவனது புலி போன்ற வீரத் தோற்றத்தைக் கண்ட பாணர்கள் ஆரவாரித்த ஒலியை விட, ஆரவாரம் மிக்க குறும்பூர் நகரில் எழுந்த அலர் (வதந்தி) மிகப் பெரியதாகும்.","explanation":"In this neytal (maritime) poem, the confidante (tōḻi) addresses the heroine, or speaks in the hearing of the secret lover, about the rising public gossip (alar). She points out that the actual days of union granted by the lord of the shore (tuṟaivaṉ) were very few, yet the rumors have grown disproportionately loud. The poem uses a vivid natural image: the waves, sounding like drums beaten with drumsticks, crash and destroy the tiny homes built by crabs in the root-hollows of the ñāḻal trees. This represents how the harsh public gossip threatens to destroy the delicate, secret love of the couple. To emphasize the scale of the gossip, the poet Paraṇar employs a historical allusion, comparing the uproar to the clamor raised by bards in the town of Kurumpur upon witnessing the fierce, tiger-like battle stance of the Vicciyar chief fighting against the kings.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.7],[0.7,1.45],[1.45,1.6],[1.6,2.2],[2.2,2.56],[2.56,2.88],[3.04,3.2],[3.2,3.2],[3.2,4.8],[4.8,5.2],[5.2,5.6],[5.6,6.6],[6.6,7.1],[7.1,7.3],[7.3,7.6],[7.6,7.6],[7.6,7.6],[7.6,7.6],[7.6,10.1],[10.1,10.77],[10.77,10.93],[10.93,11.27],[11.27,12.1],[12.1,12.9],[12.9,13.5],[13.5,13.9],[13.9,14.5],[14.5,14.8],[14.8,15.2],[15.2,16.1]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.7],[1.7,2.0],[2.0,2.9],[2.9,3.38],[3.38,3.7],[3.7,4.1],[5.1,5.6],[5.6,5.6],[5.6,5.6],[5.6,5.6],[5.6,5.6],[5.6,5.6],[5.6,7.64],[7.64,9.0],[9.0,9.0],[9.0,9.0],[9.0,9.0],[9.0,9.0],[9.0,12.5],[12.5,13.0],[13.1,13.6],[13.6,14.0],[14.0,14.53],[14.67,15.6],[15.6,16.0],[16.0,16.6],[16.6,16.9],[16.9,17.4],[17.4,18.3]]}}